# CodeRabbit review conventions

**Why this file:** [CodeRabbit](https://docs.coderabbit.ai/) runs on PRs using [`.coderabbit.yaml`](../../.coderabbit.yaml) (`path_instructions`, assertive profile, `enable_prompt_for_ai_agents` for inline “AI agent” hints). This rule does **not** replace that config — it tells **Cursor agents** to treat the same YAML + [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) as the source of truth so local edits match what the bot will flag.

**Before PR:** Prefer `cr review --agent --base main` when you use the CodeRabbit CLI; fix high-confidence issues, skip noise with a short reason, keep diffs small, run the **allowed** `npm run` checks from AGENTS.md.

**Stack specifics** live in other rules — do not duplicate them here: `nextjs-node-server-2026.mdc`, `next-intl-single-locale-routing.mdc`, `react-form-events.mdc`, `ui-color-tokens.mdc`, `admin-list-usability.mdc`, `tdd.mdc`, `e2e-verification.mdc`.

**CodeRabbit config:** [`.coderabbit.yaml`](../../.coderabbit.yaml) `path_instructions` include URL-shape guidance (default no `trailingSlash`; use `/path#hash` not `/path/#hash` for assertions and in-app links) so the bot does not repeat mistaken `/ratings/#…` review suggestions.
